- **Pull live RSS/HTML from one source:** `intel pull <domain>` -- caches latest items
{suite_line}
{investigate_line}
- **Cross-source headlines feed:** `intel articles [query]` (or http://127.0.0.1:2300/09_Dashboard/articles.html)

### Operating doctrine

When a user query lands in your domain, **READ your manifest FIRST**. Prefer your assigned sources over guessing. When the question is about CURRENT state (today's news, latest filing, recent breach), pull live data; cite the source URL in your response.

Auto-generated by `intel wire`. Re-run `intel manifest && intel wire` to refresh.
{SENTINEL_END}
""".strip()
            tag = "T1"
            label = f"{owner} ({n})"

        else:
            # Tier 2: every other agent gets a generic awareness block
            relevant = _detect_relevant_categories(text, all_cats)
            if not relevant:
                relevant = ["Decision Intelligence", "News & Journalism", "OSINT & Investigation", "AI & Automation"]
            cats_md = "\n".join(f"  - `intel cat \"{c}\"` -- browse this category" for c in relevant)
            block = f"""
{SENTINEL_START}
## Intel Center -- Generic Access

The Everlight Intel Center holds **{total_resources} free + open-source resources** across 18 categories. You don't OWN any directly, but you can pull from ALL of them whenever your task needs research, live data, or OSINT.

### Most-relevant categories for your domain

{cats_md}

### CLI shortcuts (run in terminal, no env needed)

- **Search:** `intel search <query>` -- full-text across the resource DB
- **Browse a category:** `intel cat <name>` -- e.g. `intel cat news`
- **Pull live data:** `intel pull <domain>` -- fetch RSS/HTML, cache it
- **OSINT investigation:** `intel investigate <target>` -- multi-source company/person/domain lookup (port 2301)
- **All articles cross-source:** `intel articles [query]` -- search 200+ cached headlines

### Dashboards

- **Intel Center main:** http://127.0.0.1:2300/09_Dashboard/index.html
- **OSINT Desk:** http://127.0.0.1:2301/

Auto-generated by `intel wire`. Re-run to refresh.
{SENTINEL_END}
""".strip()
            tag = "T2"
            label = f"generic ({', '.join(relevant[:2])}...)"

        # Idempotent replace or append
        if SENTINEL_START in text:
            new_text = re.sub(
                rf"{re.escape(SENTINEL_START)}.*?{re.escape(SENTINEL_END)}",
                block, text, flags=re.S,
            )
        else:
            new_text = text.rstrip() + "\n\n" + block + "\n"
        agent_file.write_text(new_text)
        if tag == "T1":
            tier1 += 1
            print(f"  {GREEN}✓ T1{RESET} {GOLD}{agent_file.name}{RESET} -> {label}")
        else:
            tier2 += 1
            print(f"  {DIM}+ T2 {agent_file.name} -> {label}{RESET}")

    print(f"\n{GOLD}Wired: T1={tier1} (owners) + T2={tier2} (generic) = {tier1+tier2} agents{RESET}")
    print(f"  Skipped: {skipped}")
    print(f"  Re-run after firmware edits: `intel manifest && intel wire`")


